Design of extractor:
- Inputs (pinned by sha256):
  - schemas/af_wcc_vacuum.yaml
  - schemas/af_scc_c2_vacuum.yaml
  - schemas/af_scc_c0_vacuum.yaml
  - research_map/formulation_taxonomy.yaml (for T1 guards)
- Normalize data_class:
  - Flatten the `data_class` mapping to leaf paths, normalizing whitespace and a small set of alias-equivalent tokens (e.g. "diffeomorphism invariant" vs "diffeomorphism-invariant"; "asymptotically the identity" vs "asymptotically-identity"; status strings differ — should status be part of the data class? The C2 `sobolev_variant` has `status` inline; WCC has `status` inside. Those are metadata/citation-status, not the data class itself. I should define a "semantic data-class core" excluding fields whose names indicate provenance/status (status, citation_status, locator, hypotheses_reconciliation) and excluding `excluded_data`/`excluded_set`? Hmm — excluded_data is semantically part of class identity (genericity), but for the transfer guard "data_class fields must match exactly", strict equality of the whole data_class block is the guard. So I should report BOTH:
    (a) strict byte-normalized equality of the full data_class subtree (value-level, with newline/whitespace normalization);
    (b) semantic-core equality after excluding provenance/status-only keys;
    (c) per-key diff table.
- Genericity: compare `kind`, `topology_or_measure`/`ambient_space` across C0/C2 (guard requires genericity_kind and genericity_topology to match exactly). WCC has its own genericity; include for completeness.
- Transfer check: T1 from taxonomy; verify the guard fields; also check C0's implication_ledger asserts the one-way entailment and C2's must_not_conflate says C0 => C2 only.
- Verdict: `data_class_strict_equal` (bool) between C0 and C2; `data_class_core_equal`; `genericity_kind_equal`; `genericity_topology_equal`; `t1_data_precondition` = all four; list of blocking diffs.
